# What the image is built from (Dockerfile), as an allowlist: everything is left out, then the
# workspace's manifests and lockfile and the packages and apps are let back in, and, within those, what
# is never the image's is left out again: installed packages and builds (the image installs its own),
# dotfiles (settings files and keys, an editor's or an assistant's local settings), env files under any
# name (ENV_FILE may name one), keys and certificates, logs, and what a server writes where it runs. A
# file only a developer's own global gitignore hides still never reaches the image. A test reads this
# file against what git tracks.
*
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!packages
!apps
**/node_modules
**/dist
# The engine package's copies of the guide and the skill, which its build writes for a packed package.
packages/dialogwright/docs
packages/dialogwright/skills
**/.*
!.npmrc
!**/.env.example
!apps/*/kb/.index
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/coverage
apps/*/traces
apps/*/audit
apps/*/sessions
packages/*/traces
packages/*/audit
packages/*/sessions
